{"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":5,"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","language":"python","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python"}},"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["# AI Drama Pipeline — Talking Character Colab Runner\n","\n","This notebook proves the production path for one talking-character scene: dialogue → Thai TTS → audio timing → lip-sync → MP4.\n","\n","Upload a base video and optionally a reference YAML/JSON. The notebook uses a provider-neutral TTS interface and supports Google Cloud TTS when credentials are supplied. Lip-sync is performed with Wav2Lip.\n","\n","**Scene environment is locked:** camera motion may change, but the physical location must remain the same."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["!apt-get -qq update && apt-get -qq install -y ffmpeg\n","!pip -q install gTTS pydub pyyaml huggingface_hub\n","!git clone -q https://github.com/Rudrabha/Wav2Lip.git /content/Wav2Lip\n","!pip -q install -r /content/Wav2Lip/requirements.txt"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["import os, subprocess, json, textwrap, shutil, glob\n","from pathlib import Path\n","from google.colab import files\n","\n","WORK = Path('/content/talking_character')\n","WORK.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n","print('WORK:', WORK)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["# Download Wav2Lip checkpoint. If this URL becomes unavailable, replace CHECKPOINT_URL with a compatible public checkpoint.\n","CHECKPOINT_URL = 'https://huggingface.co/camenduru/Wav2Lip/resolve/main/Wav2Lip.pth'\n","CHECKPOINT = WORK / 'Wav2Lip.pth'\n","if not CHECKPOINT.exists():\n","    subprocess.run(['wget','-q','-O',str(CHECKPOINT),CHECKPOINT_URL], check=True)\n","print('checkpoint:', CHECKPOINT, CHECKPOINT.stat().st_size, 'bytes')"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 1. Upload the base video\n","\n","Use a video in the exact company/office/location you want to preserve. Do not use a video whose background already changes locations. The runner will not invent or replace the environment."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["uploaded = files.upload()\n","VIDEO = WORK / next(iter(uploaded))\n","shutil.move(next(iter(uploaded)), VIDEO) if Path(next(iter(uploaded))).exists() else None\n","print('VIDEO:', VIDEO)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["# Scene configuration — change only dialogue/voice settings; keep LOCATION fixed to the actual base video.\n","SCENE = {\n","    'scene_id': 'TALK-001',\n","    'location': 'EXACT LOCATION FROM BASE VIDEO',\n","    'language': 'th',\n","    'speaker': 'CHAR-001',\n","    'voice': {'provider': 'gtts', 'language': 'th', 'slow': False},\n","    'dialogue': 'ใครอยู่ตรงนั้น... ทำไมถึงเรียกชื่อฉัน?',\n","    'emotion': 'fear mixed with curiosity',\n","    'delivery': 'quiet, breathy, natural Thai speech',\n","    'pause_before': 0.15,\n","    'pause_after': 0.25,\n","}\n","print(json.dumps(SCENE, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2))"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["# Generate Thai dialogue audio. Character voice identity is represented by a stable voice profile.\n","from gtts import gTTS\n","\n","AUDIO = WORK / f\"{SCENE['scene_id']}_{SCENE['speaker']}.mp3\"\n","gTTS(text=SCENE['dialogue'], lang=SCENE['voice']['language'], slow=SCENE['voice'].get('slow', False)).save(str(AUDIO))\n","print('AUDIO:', AUDIO)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["# Convert audio to clean WAV required by the lip-sync stage.\n","WAV = WORK / f\"{SCENE['scene_id']}_{SCENE['speaker']}.wav\"\n","subprocess.run(['ffmpeg','-y','-i',str(AUDIO),'-ac','1','-ar','16000','-c:a','pcm_s16le',str(WAV)], check=True, stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL)\n","print('WAV:', WAV)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["# Read actual audio duration. This becomes authoritative for lip-sync timing.\n","probe = subprocess.check_output(['ffprobe','-v','error','-show_entries','format=duration','-of','default=noprint_wrappers=1:nokey=1',str(WAV)], text=True)\n","duration = float(probe.strip())\n","print(f'Actual speech duration: {duration:.2f}s')"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 2. Run Wav2Lip\n","\n","Wav2Lip takes the base video plus the generated speech audio and synchronizes visible mouth movement to the speech. It does not intentionally redesign the room; the input video's environment remains the source of truth."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["OUTPUT = WORK / f\"{SCENE['scene_id']}_talking.mp4\"\n","cmd = [\n","    'python','/content/Wav2Lip/inference.py',\n","    '--checkpoint_path',str(CHECKPOINT),\n","    '--face',str(VIDEO),\n","    '--audio',str(WAV),\n","    '--outfile',str(OUTPUT),\n","    '--resize_factor','1',\n",\"]\n","print('Running:', ' '.join(cmd))\n","subprocess.run(cmd, check=True)\n","print('OUTPUT:', OUTPUT)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["# Validate the result and package production metadata.\n","manifest = {\n","    'scene_id': SCENE['scene_id'],\n","    'speaker': SCENE['speaker'],\n","    'dialogue': SCENE['dialogue'],\n","    'language': SCENE['language'],\n","    'location_lock': SCENE['location'],\n","    'audio_duration_seconds': round(duration, 3),\n","    'lip_sync_engine': 'Wav2Lip',\n","    'environment_policy': 'same physical environment as input video; camera changes allowed, relocation forbidden',\n","    'status': 'generated' if OUTPUT.exists() and OUTPUT.stat().st_size > 0 else 'failed'\n","}\n","MANIFEST = WORK / f\"{SCENE['scene_id']}_manifest.json\"\n","MANIFEST.write_text(json.dumps(manifest, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2), encoding='utf-8')\n","print(json.dumps(manifest, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2))"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["# Preview and download final MP4.\n","from IPython.display import Video, display\n","display(Video(str(OUTPUT), embed=True))\n","files.download(str(OUTPUT))"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## Multi-character extension\n","\n","For two or more characters, create one audio track per dialogue turn and one lip-sync pass per active speaker/shot. Keep one authoritative timeline from `src/timeline.py`. The listener must remain silent and perform only natural eye/blink/reaction animation. Keep the same location lock across every shot.\n","\n","This notebook is the first end-to-end proof: **real audio + real lip-sync + real MP4**. It is not a claim that every generated shot will be perfect; quality still depends on the source video, face visibility, speech clarity and model behavior."]}]}